          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Backpressure For Free"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "for await (const row of rows) {",
            "  await db.insert(row)  // throttles source",
            "}   // loop body time = the brake"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Generators As Stages"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An async generator is a Transform in disguise",
            "Legal directly as a pipeline stage",
            "Often clearer than a Transform subclass"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "Readable.from(cursor())  // DB cursor",
            "Readable.from(pages())   // paginated API",
            "// any async iterable becomes a stream"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Iterator Helpers"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "await readable",
            "  .filter(r => r.ok)",
            "  .map(r => fetch(r.url), { concurrency: 4 })",
            "  .toArray()   // also .take(), .reduce()"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Helper",
            "Gives"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "map / filter",
              "per-item, concurrency opt"
            ],
            [
              "take",
              "first n items"
            ],
            [
              "reduce / toArray",
              "collect to a value"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. The Trade-off"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Object mode costs more per chunk — no batched Buffers",
            "But record-oriented code gets far simpler",
            "For raw bytes, stay out of object mode"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Memory Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Ignoring write()'s return — memory grows unbounded",
            "Only shows in production, at scale",
            "Huge highWaterMark to fix slowness hides backpressure",
            "Collect-then-concat is a buffered read with extra steps"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Wiring Mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "pipe with no per-stage handler leaves dest open forever",
            "Missing push(null) or _flush — consumer hangs on end",
            "Callback twice throws ERR_MULTIPLE_CALLBACK",
            "Mixing paused and flowing loses chunks"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Timing Traps, Stream Types & Defaults",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Timing Mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Peeking with data, piping later — first chunks gone",
            "Fix: a PassThrough tee, or pause() first",
            "finish is not on disk — wait for close or fsync",
            "On req close, destroy the source or it reads into nowhere",
            "await inside a data handler = unbounded concurrency"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Boundaries lie",
          "text": "A JSON object or UTF-8 char split across two chunks corrupts the parse. Buffer the remainder, or setEncoding."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Type Table",
